From 8230e6fefeacfed2dd878797b17d0c839ab579b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] app: the config's ARDOP bandwidth is the widest, also for a
 gateway listed wider (OpenX6X00)

The gateway list fills in each gateway's widest ARDOP bandwidth
(bw=2000MAX for one listed as ARDOP 2000), the connect dialog takes it
over and the browser remembers it, and a connection's bw= wins over
ardop.arq_bandwidth, which the radio's Winlink page sets. On the radio
(7 W at most) 500 and 200 Hz sessions connected where 2000MAX did not.

Connect() now lowers an ARDOP bw= above the config's Max to <Max>MAX
and says so in the log; a gateway that runs a wider bandwidth takes it
and the session is negotiated down. A bw= at or under the limit, or
none, is left as it is; one that is not a bandwidth is left for the
dialer to refuse. With a test (app/ardop_bandwidth_test.go).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 app/ardop_bandwidth.go      | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 app/ardop_bandwidth_test.go | 52 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 app/connect.go              |  6 +++++
 3 files changed, 95 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 app/ardop_bandwidth.go
